A||||19||skitime||Decision Time-Stock Black Trim or Monochrome Red 88 GT T-Top||||1||
Z||000000||skitime||03-27-2001||11:08 AM||||Okay,I need help making a decision. My red 88 GT t-top is going to the paint shop on Monday. I am going to paint it the orginal bright red color. The car has Beechwood interior, gold wheels and real Mecham scoops made of orginal urethane not fiberglass. I can't decide whether to keep it stock except actual Mecham scoops or paint the black trim red too. I have seen pictures of red monochrome cars but not with T-tops. The t-tops have a lot of black framing which could be painted red but I didn't think that would look good. I was thinking of painting the black trim, mirrors, and the inside quarter window surround but not the engine grates. That would leave the t-top framing and engine grates black.<BR> <BR>Please let me know what you think. If anyone has pictures of monochrome red GTs please post them or email me them if you have trouble posting, especially if it is a t-top or any t-top monochrome Fiero for that matter.<P>Thanks<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||TheFiero64||03-27-2001||12:50 PM||||I say stick with the black trim. I like it better.<P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://people.ne.mediaone.net/fiero64/Fiero642.jpg"> <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Standard||03-27-2001||12:57 PM||||I agree, stay with the black trim.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Alex4mula||03-27-2001||01:05 PM||||Well everyone has its own opinion. I think that GTs with monotone scheme looks awesome in any bright color. I would do it. Try to see some pictures to see how nice they look.||||reg||1
Z||000004||87GT||03-27-2001||01:16 PM||||I say definately keep it black.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000005||banditbalz||03-27-2001||01:41 PM||||I say keep the trim black. It will give your ride a lower look (car will look tall with no beltline). I had to make the same decision 8 months ago and I chose black trim. Glad I did. I think the car looks more modern with the sideview mirrors painted though!<P>------------------<BR>Silver 86 GT<BR>completely stock,<BR>completely fast!||||reg||4
Z||000006||1FST2M6||03-27-2001||01:47 PM||||black trim and black a-pillars! BBBAD GT let me borrow his cars black roof.. and as a T-top it would be even sweeter! very 308/328-esque. <BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/1fsthydrant.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/1fsthydrant.jpg</A> <P>||||reg||1
Z||000007||LZeitgeist||03-27-2001||01:51 PM||||Black trim. ||||reg||1
Z||000008||skitime||03-27-2001||01:55 PM||||Here is a link to a good example of a red monochrome of forum member Contra's car <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/003310.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/003310.html</A> <P>Here is a good example of the stock red t-top of forum member RossT's car. <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/003403.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/003403.html</A> <P>I use RossT's car as my wallpaper to inspire me to get mine to look as good as his.<BR><p>[This message has been edited by skitime (edited 03-27-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000009||TheFiero64||03-27-2001||02:15 PM||||That's funny, I also use RossT's car as my desktop wallpaper  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> It is the sweetest looking GT that I've seen.<P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://people.ne.mediaone.net/fiero64/Fiero642.jpg"> <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||10
Z||000010||Veronica's V6 GT||03-27-2001||10:18 PM||||bump||||reg||1
Z||000011||fyerstarter||03-27-2001||10:25 PM||||I would have to go with the monochrome. I think that black moldings give it a less exotic look. If you look at any high end sports car (corvette, viper, ferrarri, etc.) You will see color coordinated moldings or none at all. However if you look at any econobox you will see the telltale gaudy plastic molding pieces. <P>They were designed so that grandmas and soccer moms dont dent their door when the open it into the light pole trying to get groceries in. That's not something that I want on my sports car. ||||reg||1
Z||000012||Eric||03-28-2001||12:52 AM||||If you go with a monochrome look, the first time you see a really clean red 88 with the stock trim, you'll kick yourself in the ass.  Straying too far from the original design is what makes the car become a reflection of you.  I can only speak for myself, but I certainly wouldn't want my ugly mug shining back at me every time I look at my car.  Besides, red with black looks slick as hell.||||reg||1
Z||000013||RossT||03-28-2001||01:00 AM||||Wow, Sounds like I need to use my car as wallpaper too..  Thanks.<P>Since your going to keep the car mostly stock and keep the stock rims, I would leave the trim black.  I also think that the car will keep a higher value and sell easier if it is kept stock (not that you want to sell it). But its your car, and you need to do what YOU want to do.<P>RossT||||reg||1
Z||000014||Tigger||03-28-2001||01:59 AM||||This was a tough choice for me as well. <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/tiggerfiero1.jpg" TARGET=_blank>Here's mine</A><P>The logic I used was to go ahead and paint the trim.  If I didn't like the look, I'd just go back to black.  Well... so far I haven't painted it black.<P>All up to you, hope this helps with ideas...<p>[This message has been edited by Tigger (edited 03-28-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000015||Wolfhound||03-28-2001||07:38 AM||||Tigger, Do you have a square on side view of your car? I noticed you didn't use ground effects on the center portion. Unusual, Looks good!  ||||reg||1
Z||000016||banditbalz||03-28-2001||07:39 PM||||Tigger, I was parked next to you at the Michigan show last summer. I have the Silver fastback. Your car looks sweet! Explains why I ended up with a second place in our class. This may sound goofy, but i think body coloured trim looks better on the notchbacks than on the fastbacks...<BR><P>------------------<BR>Silver 86 GT<BR>completely stock,<BR>completely fast!||||reg||1
Z||000017||Tigger||03-29-2001||12:42 AM||||Wolfhound, Thanks <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/tiggerfiero5.jpg" TARGET=_blank>here's a side view.</A>  My Uncle has a Yellow Fiero without the GT rocker trim.  I liked his so much I did the same on mine.<P>bandit, hey cool, I remember you and you're car from the show!  That's odd, I thought your car was the best fastback in our class and for sure in top three.  The judging had to have been close, your GT was Very Nice!<P>skitme, have you made a decision yet?<p>[This message has been edited by Tigger (edited 03-29-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000018||Kelvin Vivian||03-29-2001||06:43 AM||||I agree with banditbalz...<P>Painted trim looks better on a notchback (with a hardtop) than on a fastback, especially after seeing pics of Tigger's car, so my vote would be for you to keep the side trim black.<P>If I had a sunroof, or a T-top, I'd be more hesitant to paint the side trim.<P><p>[This message has been edited by Kelvin Vivian (edited 03-29-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000019||Wolfhound||03-29-2001||06:58 AM||||Thanks Tigger, That is sharp!||||reg||1
